@startuml tutorial-line-resolution
' purpose: Tutorial coach-line pipeline — deep-link
'   canonicalization, ranked beat pick,
'   intro hold with turn-open re-baseline, and
'   settled-board auto-advance gates.
' covers: apps/starchess/src/tutorial/tutorialScript.ts
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/menu-flow.puml
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/architecture/storybook-projection.puml
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/tutorial/coach-line.puml
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/tutorial/lesson-gates.puml
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

title StarChess · Tutorial line resolution

actor Player
participant "TutorialScreen" as SCREEN <<app>>
participant "tutorialScript.ts" as RESOLVER <<app>>
database "tutorialScript.config.ts" as CATALOG <<db>>
participant "Live lesson board" as BOARD <<app>>

== Deep link ==
Player ARROW_MAIN SCREEN : open /tutorial/<section>/<story>
SCREEN ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : parseTutorialSection(raw)
RESOLVER ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : fold aliases, default fog
SCREEN ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : resolveTutorialStoryId\n(first-story fallback)
RESOLVER ARROW_MAIN CATALOG : tutorialStage /\ntutorialStory lookup
RESOLVER ARROW_ERROR SCREEN : lessonBoard throws\non unknown id

== Coach line per frame ==
BOARD ARROW_MAIN SCREEN : scfen · phase · targeting
SCREEN ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : resolveTutorialLine(ctx)
RESOLVER ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : pickBeat: priority,\nthen specificity
RESOLVER ARROW_OPTIONAL SCREEN : story intro fallback
SCREEN ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : holdTutorialLine(hold,\nkey, raw, ctx)
RESOLVER ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : baseline, re-baseline,\nsticky-or-silence

== Auto-advance on a settled board ==
BOARD ARROW_QUEUE SCREEN : timeline idle + live scfen
SCREEN ARROW_MAIN RESOLVER : matchesTutorialCompleteWhen
RESOLVER ARROW_OPTIONAL SCREEN : scfen | queue | typewriter
SCREEN ARROW_MAIN SCREEN : ending hold, success\nbubble, auto-advance

' N_PRECEDENCE:
note over RESOLVER
  Per field (say, mark), the matching beat
  with the highest priority wins, then the one
  with the most leaf gates (turn, phase, each
  and() leaf); declaration order breaks only a
  full tie. `turn:` reads the SCFEN turn field,
  so a beat's turn comes from the wire, not a
  host counter. Unmatched contexts fall back
  to the story introduction comment.
end note

' N_ALERTS:
note over BOARD
  Alert rings: a beat's alertSquares, or a
  latch. `king` pins the ring to scripted
  sightings; `cc` adds the enemy Command
  Center's last seen square to every beat's
  alerts and moves it only when that square
  is visible (nextCCSighting, withCCAlert).
  ccThreat alerts visible attackers of the
  ally Command Center; fogged ones never count.
end note

' N_REBASE:
note over RESOLVER
  Turn-open bookkeeping refills gas and
  settles pending check damage, displacing
  scfen from the seed on mount. The hold
  re-baselines on check application and
  tracks undefined so resets release it.
end note

' N_STICKY:
note over RESOLVER
  Reaction lines latch sticky and retire the
  introduction; later board motion replays the
  reaction. Motion with no stored reaction
  yields silence, never a revived introduction.
end note

' N_GATES:
note over RESOLVER
  Auto-advance judges only settled boards,
  matching scfen, queue, or typewriter beats.
  Elapsed gates never evaluate live; the screen
  timer owns them, and seeds never satisfy
  their own gate.
end note

note over CATALOG
  Unknown lesson identifiers throw at lookup
  so mistyped stories surface instead of
  mounting empty boards. Section aliases
  canonicalize, with fog as the default section.
end note

note over SCREEN
  One advance delay serves every lesson,
  because the countdown affords navigation
  rather than carrying content. Closing lines
  hold at prose pace between 1.2 and 4
  seconds; absent lines skip the hold.
end note

@enduml
